  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider and adjust the probability of outcomes below 20% (here, the 10% chance of 0 in Lottery B) by increasing it to 20%, and then to compute the weighted sum of outcomes. However, the individual did not consider the low-probability outcome (0 Euros in B) in any special way, nor did they adjust probabilities or compute weighted sums. Instead, their justification focused solely on the higher probability of winning a positive amount in B (90% vs. 45%), which is a different heuristic—favoring higher chance of any gain, regardless of magnitude. This is not equivalent to the decision reason, which explicitly weights low-probability outcomes differently and computes a sum based on adjusted probabilities. The information considered by the individual (high probability of non-zero outcome in B) does not match the information required by the reason (adjusted probability of low-probability outcomes). The justification also does not align with the rule of the reason (weighted sum comparison). Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
